\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.16}{\ignorespaces KITSUNE on the \texttt  {W64 H128} base (CE 0.6537). $B'/K$ is the number of L1 micro-buckets per macro-expert. Best expert CE is the cross-entropy of the strongest expert on the positions assigned to it. The gain column is $(0.6537 - \text  {best expert CE}) / 0.6537$. It uses the full-base CE as the reference, so it is not a same-bucket comparison against the base head. The routed mixture CE is the separate column.}}{72}{table.caption.41}\protected@file@percent }
